After perhaps 25 to 30 years of testing,

00:35:38.090 --> 00:35:43.370
we've now realized that we're not apt to find a kind of magic bullet, as it were, for cancer,

00:35:43.410 --> 00:35:46.000
because cancer is so many different diseases,

00:35:46.000 --> 00:35:50.340
and each cancer in each different organ is different to the others

00:35:50.340 --> 00:35:52.740
and doesn't respond to the same sorts of drugs.

00:35:53.750 --> 00:35:58.870
We're going to look for agents which are highly selected for specific types of cancer.

00:36:00.000 --> 00:36:05.910
So we'll be screening for agents against lung cancer, colon cancer, breast cancer,

00:36:06.050 --> 00:36:11.790
and looking for agents which affect those specific types of cells and not other cells in the body.

00:36:13.930 --> 00:36:20.310
The Natural Products Division of the NCI is extending its search for new anti-cancer agents beyond the plant kingdom.

00:36:25.000 --> 00:36:28.720
Recently, they've carried their exploration for natural medicines to the sea.

00:36:31.600 --> 00:36:41.160
One promising discovery comes not from a plant, but from a marine animal called a tunicate or sea squirt, Dr. Kenneth Reinhart.

